GettingStarted: {
	Text:
		'''
		Welcome to the Arcane Odyssey Mod. To get started, find your [i:ArcaneOdyssey/EagleLegacy] Eagle Legacy. Using it will allow you to select your power.

		[i:ArcaneOdyssey/BasicCombat] Fighting Styles like Basic Combat allow you to use melee style techniques.

		[i:ArcaneOdyssey/FireMagic] Magic Types allow you to cast spells using scrolls, and are highly versatile.

		[i:ArcaneOdyssey/EaglePatrimony] Relics allow you to summon phenomena using the power of creation, focusing your minions.
		'''
	DisplayName: Getting Started
}

MagicTypes: {
	Text:
		'''
		You have obtained a magic type. With this you can cast powerful spells, and greatly enhance weapons.

		But for now, try left clicking with your magic. This will shoot a basic blast, which isn't too powerful.
		'''
	DisplayName: Magic Types
}

AboutGodSouls: {
	Text:
		'''
		You have been granted a portion of a god's soul. With this, you can enhance your [i:ArcaneOdyssey/SpiritEnergy] Relics.

		Select a soul using the Cycle God Soul keybind.

		Some relics synergize with souls, modifying their stats.

		Other relics may be unstable with an incompatible soul. You may take damage when using these, and the stats are lopsided.
		'''
	DisplayName: God Souls
}

FightingStyles: {
	Text:
		'''
		You have obtained a fighting style. With this, you can unleash skilled techniques, and wield weapons far too heavy for a regular person.

		But for now, try left clicking with your fighting style. This will unleash a basic strike, which isn't too powerful.

		[i:ArcaneOdyssey/BasicCombat] Basic Combat can be upgraded into other fighting styles. Try giving it to the Guide NPC to see what you can craft with it!
		'''
	DisplayName: Fighting Styles
}

ForgingBronze: {
	Text:
		'''
		[i:ArcaneOdyssey/BronzeBar] Bronze is a material used primarily by a certain nation. It combines [i:20]/[i:703], [i:19]/[i:706], and [i:86]/[i:1329] at a [i:221] Hellforge.

		Old weapons can be upgraded using [i:ArcaneOdyssey/BronzeBar] to add abilities, and [i:ArcaneOdyssey/RavennaChest] heavy armour can be forged with it.
		'''
	DisplayName: Forging Bronze
}

Imbuing: {
	Text:
		'''
		Magic types, Fighting Styles, and Relics are all imbues, and thus can all be imbued into compatible ranged/melee weapons.

		This can be done by right clicking with your imbue to select it, or you can choose an imbue per item using the Cycle Item Imbue keybind.

		Imbued items normally use the Imbue stats of your imbue, rebalancing the stats of the item slightly. Debuffs from your imbue are also applied to the item.

		To imbue compatible accessories, you must right click the magic to select it as your primary imbue.
		'''
	DisplayName: Imbuing
}

Mutating: {
	DisplayName: Mutating
	Text: 
		'''
		Congrats. You have located a [i:ArcaneOdyssey/HecateShard] shard of Hecate.

		With this, you can evolve your magic to the next level, Lost Magic.

		There are many options for mutating your magic. Almost all lost magic have unique gimmicks, which will determine your playstyle.
		'''
}

ObtainingScrolls: {
	DisplayName: Obtaining Scrolls
	Text:
		'''
		[i:ArcaneOdyssey/EmptyScroll] Scrolls are a medium for directly channeling your imbue.

		As you progress, more powerful scrolls become obtainable using these methods.

		The easiest way to find scrolls is by breaking scrolls underground. This has a pity system, making scrolls more common with every pot you break.

		The second method is fishing. All crates have a chance of granting scrolls of any tier.

		The final way is to naturally find scrolls in chests. This will only yield common scrolls, making it obsolete later.
		'''
}

